WEBVTT

1
00:00:27.491 --> 00:00:29.201
Your father's in danger.

2
00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:37.209
Special Agent Billie Rand. FBI.

3
00:00:38.001 --> 00:00:39.503
I don't talk to cops.

4
00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.215
They're gonna kill him. Lucky.

5
00:00:51.974 --> 00:00:53.267
Here's what I know.

6
00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.020
Priscilla buys gas. wholesale.

7
00:00:57.104 --> 00:00:59.231
She doesn't pay state taxes.

8
00:01:00.023 --> 00:01:04.443
She then resells it
through shell companies for full price.

9
00:01:05.027 --> 00:01:06.321
That's what I know.

10
00:01:06.405 --> 00:01:11.201
What I don't have is anything
that connects her to that scam.

11
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.874
What she's very good at
is making other people take the fall.

12
00:01:17.875 --> 00:01:20.085
Guess who the fall guy is.

13
00:01:23.213 --> 00:01:28.927
I have enough to put Cary and John away
for the next ten years.

14
00:01:29.011 --> 00:01:30.762
If that were true.
you would have done it already.

15
00:01:33.015 --> 00:01:34.725
Unless there's a reason that I haven't.

16
00:01:37.978 --> 00:01:39.605
Okay. so you only want Priscilla.

17
00:01:39.688 --> 00:01:41.023
And Whittaker.

18
00:01:41.106 --> 00:01:42.774
And I know you want the same thing.

19
00:01:42.858 --> 00:01:44.276
You don't know anything about what I want.

20
00:01:45.736 --> 00:01:46.945
I know that before this.

21
00:01:47.029 --> 00:01:49.114
you and your father
were strictly small-time.

22
00:01:49.198 --> 00:01:55.704
I know that you know that your daddy
is in over his head with Priscilla.

23
00:01:55.787 --> 00:01:58.999
And I know that you wanna get her out
of his life.

24
00:02:01.335 --> 00:02:02.711
So what would you have me do?

25
00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.423
Help me take the bull's-eye
off your father's back.

26
00:02:06.924 --> 00:02:09.843
Putting Priscilla behind bars
may be the only way to keep him safe.

27
00:02:09.927 --> 00:02:11.512
You can't guarantee that.

28
00:02:11.595 --> 00:02:14.848
No. But I can keep him out of prison…

29
00:02:16.141 --> 00:02:18.101
if you help me take her down.

30
00:02:21.939 --> 00:02:23.023
I can't.

31
00:02:24.566 --> 00:02:25.567
No.

32
00:02:25.651 --> 00:02:26.652
You sure?

33
00:02:27.402 --> 00:02:30.364
Yeah. I've been chasing Priscilla.
but I've been watching you.

34
00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:33.450
And all your life. you've been…

35
00:02:37.162 --> 00:02:39.373
playing the hand you were dealt.

36
00:02:40.499 --> 00:02:43.627
This is an opportunity for you
to get out of this shit.

37
00:02:44.169 --> 00:02:46.213
To play with a fresh deck.

38
00:02:46.755 --> 00:02:48.173
What about Cary?

39
00:02:49.925 --> 00:02:51.677
Depends on how deep he goes.

40
00:02:54.763 --> 00:02:55.848
Full immunity.

41
00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:00.185
For my dad and for Cary or else no deal.

42
00:03:04.022 --> 00:03:05.023
Girl.

43
00:03:07.192 --> 00:03:08.527
You ask for a lot.

44
00:03:11.405 --> 00:03:12.406
So do you.

45
00:04:47.751 --> 00:04:48.919
You're alive.

46
00:04:54.675 --> 00:04:55.676
Good for you.

47
00:04:56.593 --> 00:04:57.970
- Lucky.
- Give me the seed phrase.

48
00:04:58.053 --> 00:04:59.596
Lucky. you gotta listen to me.

49
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.850
No. The seed phrase. Please.

50
00:05:04.017 --> 00:05:06.395
Lucky.
Listen. I need to explain. all right?

51
00:05:06.478 --> 00:05:07.938
Can I explain?

52
00:05:08.021 --> 00:05:09.314
Don't!

53
00:05:11.233 --> 00:05:12.234
Fuck.

54
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.752
No. I don't want your fucking ice.

55
00:05:40.429 --> 00:05:43.932
Sorry. I knew you would find me.
I just didn't think it would be this soon.

56
00:05:44.683 --> 00:05:46.685
I think we're experiencing time
a little differently.

57
00:05:46.768 --> 00:05:48.395
Okay. well. whatever happened. I'm sorry.

58
00:05:48.478 --> 00:05:49.646
I understand. okay?

59
00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:51.231
What? Don't do that.

60
00:05:51.315 --> 00:05:52.858
- No.
- What?

61
00:05:52.941 --> 00:05:55.360
Don't do the thing that you do
where you try and appease me

62
00:05:55.444 --> 00:05:56.862
before you even know
what the fuck you did.

63
00:05:56.945 --> 00:05:58.739
- I know what the fuck I did.
- Oh. no. you don't.

64
00:05:58.822 --> 00:06:01.450
- Lucky…
- You made me a fucking mark. Cary!

65
00:06:01.533 --> 00:06:03.327
- No. that's not what happened.
- Bullshit!

66
00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:04.995
- I didn't have a choice.
- Bullshit again!

67
00:06:05.078 --> 00:06:06.079
Can I explain myself?

68
00:06:06.163 --> 00:06:07.164
No. I don't wanna hear it.

69
00:06:07.247 --> 00:06:09.082
I know you don't.
but I think you fucking need to right now.

70
00:06:09.166 --> 00:06:11.293
No. I know you've had as much time
to rehearse for this moment

71
00:06:11.376 --> 00:06:12.377
as I've spent picturing it.

72
00:06:12.461 --> 00:06:14.838
So I am sure you've
got a great story loaded up

73
00:06:14.922 --> 00:06:16.298
and ready to go. but I really don't want--

74
00:06:16.381 --> 00:06:17.508
I will hit you again!

75
00:06:17.591 --> 00:06:19.468
Okay. Fuck.

76
00:06:22.221 --> 00:06:24.515
Maybe go for a softer area this time.

77
00:06:25.307 --> 00:06:28.685
Are you seriously trying
to be fucking charming right now?

78
00:06:28.769 --> 00:06:30.187
I'm not. This is hard for me too. okay?

79
00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.439
Of course. this is hard for you.

80
00:06:32.523 --> 00:06:34.191
Yes. let's make this about you…

81
00:06:34.274 --> 00:06:36.109
- That's not what I meant.
- …and your obvious misery.

82
00:06:36.193 --> 00:06:37.861
I was terrified. Cary.

83
00:06:38.362 --> 00:06:41.365
Okay? I didn't know
whether I had to be hating you

84
00:06:41.448 --> 00:06:44.868
or grieving you
or fucking somehow saving you.

85
00:06:44.952 --> 00:06:46.620
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
- Don't!

86
00:06:48.205 --> 00:06:49.831
You know. at first. I thought that maybe

87
00:06:49.915 --> 00:06:51.542
something had been done
to both of us. right?

88
00:06:51.625 --> 00:06:55.170
Like maybe we were both drugged.
and you were hurt or worse.

89
00:06:55.254 --> 00:06:58.382
and I was gonna have to spend the rest of
my life never knowing what had happened.

90
00:06:58.465 --> 00:06:59.633
But after a while. I realized

91
00:06:59.716 --> 00:07:02.010
that the only possibility
that I could actually accept

92
00:07:02.094 --> 00:07:03.762
was that you were dead.

93
00:07:04.388 --> 00:07:07.266
Because at least if you were dead then
that means that you did not do this to me.

94
00:07:07.349 --> 00:07:10.060
But here you are alive and well
in a fucking beach house.

95
00:07:10.143 --> 00:07:11.436
and you did do this to me.

96
00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:16.567
We've got a hit on the plates and
IDed Masterson at the house in La Jolla.

97
00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.443
We've got local cops moving in.

98
00:07:18.527 --> 00:07:21.405
but I'm requesting all federal agents
in the area.

99
00:07:21.488 --> 00:07:24.324
All available units.
report back to the station

100
00:07:24.408 --> 00:07:26.368
to assist an FBI fugitive task force.

101
00:07:26.451 --> 00:07:28.203
Please indicate then switch to four.

102
00:07:28.996 --> 00:07:31.373
Fugitive task force?
Do you think that's him?

103
00:07:31.999 --> 00:07:33.250
We'll know soon enough.

104
00:07:34.585 --> 00:07:35.794
What a mess.

105
00:07:36.753 --> 00:07:38.255
We've cleaned up worse.

106
00:07:39.631 --> 00:07:41.091
Remember Temple City?

107
00:07:41.175 --> 00:07:43.427
Oh. God. I think I blocked that.

108
00:07:43.969 --> 00:07:46.013
The point is. we walked out of there.

109
00:07:47.598 --> 00:07:51.560
You and I have walked out a lot of places
that no one should have walked out of.

110
00:07:51.643 --> 00:07:54.354
Yes. but this is Cary. okay.
He's not like us.

111
00:07:54.855 --> 00:07:56.690
I still have to kill spiders for him.

112
00:07:56.773 --> 00:07:58.066
Drive faster. please.

113
00:08:02.696 --> 00:08:04.531
I know how this looks. okay?

114
00:08:04.615 --> 00:08:07.159
And part of the reason it looks that way
is because it is that way.

115
00:08:07.242 --> 00:08:08.577
I can't deny that.

116
00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.121
And I'm not gonna sit here
and try and excuse what I've done.

117
00:08:11.205 --> 00:08:13.999
But I've had some time to think about it.
and even now…

118
00:08:14.499 --> 00:08:16.627
even now. standing here with you.

119
00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:20.047
I don't know if I would have been able
to do things any differently. okay?

120
00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.382
And believe me. however much you hate me

121
00:08:22.466 --> 00:08:23.675
right now in this moment.

122
00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:26.970
it doesn't even… it doesn't fucking
compare to how much I hate myself for it.

123
00:08:27.054 --> 00:08:28.889
I think you might
be underestimating me. honey.

124
00:08:28.972 --> 00:08:31.391
- Don't say that.
- Well. I don't know who you are.

125
00:08:31.475 --> 00:08:33.143
- Yes. you do. You know me.
- Cary. no. I don't.

126
00:08:33.227 --> 00:08:34.602
The person I know wouldn't do this.

127
00:08:34.686 --> 00:08:36.563
You're the only person
who's ever known me. Lucky.

128
00:08:36.647 --> 00:08:37.648
Clearly.

129
00:08:40.317 --> 00:08:41.902
Look. I made a mistake.

130
00:08:41.985 --> 00:08:43.237
I know I made a mistake.

131
00:08:43.862 --> 00:08:45.489
But you're not gonna stand there
and convince me

132
00:08:45.572 --> 00:08:47.407
that what we have isn't real. okay?

133
00:08:47.491 --> 00:08:50.035
I fell in love with you
two seconds after I saw you.

134
00:08:50.118 --> 00:08:52.371
- And asking you to marry me--
- Okay. so when did the lies start?

135
00:08:52.454 --> 00:08:53.872
- What?
- Well. was it before the wedding?

136
00:08:53.956 --> 00:08:55.582
- No. That was all real.
- After the wedding?

137
00:08:55.666 --> 00:08:58.210
I know it might be difficult
to pinpoint an exact date.

138
00:08:58.293 --> 00:09:01.046
but I'm just trying to get a general
picture of when my life became a lie--

139
00:09:01.129 --> 00:09:02.506
She was going to kill you!

140
00:09:03.841 --> 00:09:05.801
My darling boy.

141
00:09:05.884 --> 00:09:07.219
Hello. Mother.

142
00:09:07.302 --> 00:09:09.096
- Look at you.
- Hello.

143
00:09:13.851 --> 00:09:15.143
I missed you.

144
00:09:22.484 --> 00:09:23.485
Come on.

145
00:09:25.445 --> 00:09:27.823
I would have visited you if you'd let me.

146
00:09:27.906 --> 00:09:29.867
I couldn't let you see me in there.

147
00:09:32.786 --> 00:09:35.414
Yeah. I just really hate
that you were in there and not Wayne.

148
00:09:35.998 --> 00:09:36.999
It's okay.

149
00:09:37.082 --> 00:09:38.083
It's not.

150
00:09:39.084 --> 00:09:40.711
Well. listen.

151
00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:45.507
All that matters is I am here now.

152
00:09:47.384 --> 00:09:48.594
Here. sit down.

153
00:09:55.017 --> 00:09:56.018
How did you get out?

154
00:09:57.477 --> 00:09:58.729
Good behavior.

155
00:09:59.354 --> 00:10:00.606
Wayne's lawyers?

156
00:10:04.568 --> 00:10:05.903
What's in it for him?

157
00:10:07.279 --> 00:10:10.532
Well. it's been brought to my attention
that there's some money missing.

158
00:10:18.123 --> 00:10:19.791
Does that have something to do with me?

159
00:10:20.375 --> 00:10:23.170
Well. John's been stealing
from me for years.

160
00:10:23.253 --> 00:10:24.463
Skimming.

161
00:10:24.546 --> 00:10:27.007
And the only person
who knows where that money is.

162
00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.509
is that little girlfriend of yours.

163
00:10:30.636 --> 00:10:32.471
- Wife.
- What?

164
00:10:35.057 --> 00:10:36.266
You're married?

165
00:10:37.768 --> 00:10:38.894
You didn't tell me?

166
00:10:38.977 --> 00:10:40.312
You wouldn't see me.

167
00:10:41.355 --> 00:10:42.356
Listen.

168
00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.567
I know it's been hard. okay?

169
00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.362
You had to do what you had to do
to survive.

170
00:10:48.445 --> 00:10:49.780
But I'm out now.

171
00:10:49.863 --> 00:10:54.618
And we're gonna get our business in order
and everything is gonna go back to normal.

172
00:10:54.701 --> 00:10:56.537
I love her. Mom.

173
00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.789
Come on. What happened to you?

174
00:10:58.872 --> 00:11:01.583
I'm gone for two years.
I don't even recognize you.

175
00:11:01.667 --> 00:11:04.169
Well. I'm happy. Maybe that's why
you don't recognize me.

176
00:11:04.253 --> 00:11:05.504
- You're not happy.
- I am.

177
00:11:05.587 --> 00:11:06.672
Look at you. You're bored.

178
00:11:07.756 --> 00:11:11.593
You're working minimum wage
and playing house with that little girl.

179
00:11:11.677 --> 00:11:13.804
You're capable of so much more.

180
00:11:15.889 --> 00:11:17.349
It's a nice life.

181
00:11:17.933 --> 00:11:18.934
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

182
00:11:19.017 --> 00:11:20.561
Is that what you want?

183
00:11:20.644 --> 00:11:21.687
A nice life?

184
00:11:22.271 --> 00:11:24.022
Man. you got a seat at the table.

185
00:11:24.106 --> 00:11:25.816
Wayne is ready to bring you into the fold.

186
00:11:25.899 --> 00:11:28.986
Wayne does not give a shit about me. okay?

187
00:11:29.069 --> 00:11:30.737
And he definitely does not
give a shit about you.

188
00:11:30.821 --> 00:11:33.574
Yeah. you bring in that money.
I promise you that's gonna change.

189
00:11:33.657 --> 00:11:35.492
I'm not doing this shit for Wayne. Mom.

190
00:11:35.576 --> 00:11:37.077
No. no. do it for yourself.

191
00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:39.955
I'm giving you a gift here.
This is a chance at a better life.

192
00:11:40.038 --> 00:11:41.164
What. like yours?

193
00:11:41.248 --> 00:11:42.791
You just got out of prison. Mom.

194
00:11:44.001 --> 00:11:45.002
Prison.

195
00:11:45.085 --> 00:11:48.255
I love that we're having
this conversation right now. I love it!

196
00:11:48.964 --> 00:11:49.965
Look.

197
00:11:51.967 --> 00:11:54.303
Look. you could do it with the girl. okay?

198
00:11:55.804 --> 00:11:58.140
All you have to do is get her
to bring it to me.

199
00:11:58.223 --> 00:11:59.224
And then we're done.

200
00:11:59.308 --> 00:12:00.601
You can live your life.

201
00:12:01.185 --> 00:12:02.352
You know. you can…

202
00:12:02.895 --> 00:12:04.897
move to Fresno and work at Starbucks.

203
00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.316
I don't know. Whatever the fuck you want.

204
00:12:09.818 --> 00:12:10.986
So you're saying no?

205
00:12:11.069 --> 00:12:12.404
- I am.
- Okay. why?

206
00:12:12.988 --> 00:12:15.490
I'm in love. Mom.

207
00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.036
I'm in love. and I know
you wouldn't understand that.

208
00:12:19.119 --> 00:12:22.998
So you're sacrificing everything
for a girl who is lying to you?

209
00:12:23.081 --> 00:12:24.541
What are you talking about?

210
00:12:24.625 --> 00:12:26.835
That girl that
you're so madly in love with.

211
00:12:26.919 --> 00:12:29.713
You were busted by the fucking feds. Mom.

212
00:12:29.796 --> 00:12:31.673
Yeah. how do you think that happened?

213
00:12:34.885 --> 00:12:36.637
- Huh?
- No. Bullshit.

214
00:12:37.262 --> 00:12:40.057
That's bullshit. okay? Her father
went down in that bust. all right.

215
00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:42.476
So did she. right?
They took her away in cuffs. right?

216
00:12:42.559 --> 00:12:44.811
Yet she was never charged.
never even interrogated.

217
00:12:44.895 --> 00:12:47.731
No. no. no.
Because she was barely involved. Mom.

218
00:12:47.814 --> 00:12:51.026
She was an accessory. Cary.
With knowledge of the organization.

219
00:12:51.109 --> 00:12:52.194
And they let her walk.

220
00:12:52.277 --> 00:12:55.322
Did it never fucking occur to you
to ask her why?

221
00:12:55.405 --> 00:12:57.324
Are you really so fucking naive?

222
00:13:07.793 --> 00:13:10.712
Lucky knows where my money is
and you're gonna bring it to me.

223
00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:16.426
You know what Wayne's gonna do to me
if I don't bring him that money?

224
00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:18.428
Are you really gonna let that happen?

225
00:13:19.304 --> 00:13:20.305
Mom.

226
00:13:20.889 --> 00:13:21.974
This is my life.

227
00:13:23.559 --> 00:13:25.727
There was a time
that meant something to you.

228
00:13:28.897 --> 00:13:30.983
You won't do it for me.
your fucking mother.

229
00:13:31.942 --> 00:13:35.153
Do it for your wife if you love her
the way you say you do.

230
00:13:35.237 --> 00:13:38.699
Because you know what happens to her
if I have to handle this myself.

231
00:13:47.374 --> 00:13:49.960
Okay? And you didn't think
to tell me any of this?

232
00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:53.046
Tell you? Tell you?

233
00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:55.591
- Are you fucking kidding me right now?
- Okay. Okay. We…

234
00:13:55.674 --> 00:13:58.051
- Don't turn it around right now.
- Don't turn it around?

235
00:13:58.135 --> 00:14:00.262
You worked with the feds
and you didn't tell me.

236
00:14:01.388 --> 00:14:03.223
You're the reason she went to prison.

237
00:14:03.307 --> 00:14:04.558
They were already on to her.

238
00:14:05.142 --> 00:14:07.436
- Bullshit.
- I had no choice.

239
00:14:07.519 --> 00:14:09.396
When I said that two minutes ago.
you said. "Bullshit."

240
00:14:09.479 --> 00:14:11.148
Well. when you said it. it was.

241
00:14:14.735 --> 00:14:18.488
You can tell yourself whatever you want.
but you know I'm right.

242
00:14:19.072 --> 00:14:20.324
You lied to me.

243
00:14:22.576 --> 00:14:24.369
I wanted to tell you…

244
00:14:24.453 --> 00:14:25.996
- But you didn't. did you?
- But--

245
00:14:26.079 --> 00:14:28.707
You had years to tell me the truth.

246
00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:29.833
Years.

247
00:14:29.917 --> 00:14:32.461
The whole time we were married.
every time I talked to you about my mom.

248
00:14:32.544 --> 00:14:34.713
you never thought to mention
that you were the one who sold her out.

249
00:14:34.796 --> 00:14:36.423
- I couldn't.
- And now you come in here

250
